ning & Skills segment provides vocational qualifications, GED, TalentLens, Faethm, Credly, Pearson College, and Enterprise content and training. The Higher Education segment engages in the US, Canadian, and international higher education courseware businesses. Pearson plc was founded in 1844 and is headquartered in London, the United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Omar Paul Abbosh | CEO &  Executive Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $346K ranks in the bottom quartile among Communication Services peers. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Pearson, Plc is a large-cap communication services business with a $10.5B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 51% confirm genuine pricing power.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 123% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.226712508254814},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (38% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["25 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(PSO) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/10/PSO_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_111326035201_1794559921.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794559921.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(PSO) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/PSO_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_110326040801_1793696881.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793696881.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Pearson (PSO) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/pearson-pso-said-q3-earnings-110238430.html","date":"2026-10-22","timestamp":1792666958.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Cou